# Citation metadata for this repository (GitHub shows a "Cite this repository"
# button from it). Zenodo reads .zenodo.json instead when both exist; keep the
# two in sync. See REPRODUCIBILITY.md for the release/DOI steps.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it using the metadata from this file."
type: software
title: "Jay Tilak Pentapati: Geographic Data Science & Engineering Portfolio"
abstract: >-
  Source of a Quarto website with eleven reproducible geographic data science
  projects in Python and R (spatial analysis, spatial econometrics,
  spatio-temporal modelling, machine learning and big-data processing), with
  pinned per-project environments, data availability notes and frozen
  computational results.
authors:
  - given-names: Jay Tilak
    family-names: Pentapati
    website: "https://tilak-pentapati.github.io"
    # orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0000-0000-0000"  # TODO: add ORCID iD once registered
repository-code: "https://github.com/tilak-pentapati/tilak-pentapati.github.io"
url: "https://tilak-pentapati.github.io"
keywords:
  - geographic data science
  - spatial analysis
  - spatial statistics
  - reproducible research
  - Quarto
  - R
  - Python
